        </div>

        <p>
            <strong>Q1. Can the same actuator be used for different aerosol products?</strong><br>
            No. Actuators must be matched to formulation properties, propellant pressure, and intended spray behavior.
            Using a generic actuator often leads to performance issues.
        </p>

        <p>
            <strong>Q2. Does actuator size affect spray rate?</strong><br>
            Yes. Orifice diameter and internal geometry directly control flow rate, atomization, and discharge velocity.
        </p>

        <p>
            <strong>Q3. Are aerosol actuators chemically resistant?</strong><br>
            Resistance depends on the polymer used. Polypropylene is common, but aggressive solvents may require
            specialized materials.
        </p>

        <p>
            <strong>Q4. When is a custom actuator necessary?</strong><br>
            Custom actuators are required when standard designs cannot achieve desired spray patterns, dosing accuracy,
            safety features, or brand differentiation.
        </p>

